<title>CHINA: HK TWO-YEAR NOTES AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD 6.43 PCT.</title>
<headline>HK TWO-YEAR NOTES AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD 6.43 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average accepted price for two-year Exchange Fund Notes tendered on Monday was 99.95 to yield 6.43 percent, the Hong Kong Monetary Authority said.</p>
<p>The lowest price accepted was 99.94 for a yield of 6.43 percent. The average price tendered was 99.91 for a yield of 6.45 percent.</p>
<p>The notes carry a coupon of 6.30 percent and mature on August 12, 1999. The HKMA said that HK$500 million was allotted.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371; Fax (852) 2845-0636</p>
